# RAD-01 same-input unit comparer source proposal

This is the existing CTF-01 actual-data comparer stage adapted to RAD-01. It is unexecuted Source only. It authenticates a successful real OriginalDataQA invocation against the held exact three reader sources, its actual 25-argument command, approved reader SHA, direct inputs and full stdout. Actual Native data, counts, fresh input-only freeze, scope and strict two-profile policy must join that review. Root must supply genuine future runtime references; this package contains no future result, build, binary, exit or numerical comparison identity.

The future command keeps the established seven options:

```text
python -X utf8 -B <compare_unit.py> --approved-source-sha256 <reviewed SHA> --original-data-review <actual path#SHA> --original-data-review-execution <actual path#SHA> --Rust-build-execution <actual path#SHA> --Rust-execution <actual path#SHA> --Rust-results <actual path#SHA> --output-dir <fresh contained RAD-01 directory>
```

OriginalDataQA must release actual complete data before Cargo starts, and Cargo must finish before the actual example executes. The unique Cargo compiler-artifact row, executable hash, target source/package path and real source-preserving command are joined to the candidate's actual full source snapshot. Its two observer and ten API source bindings must match that capture. The actual executable command has the five input-only arguments documented in the held candidate observer. The comparer rehashes only the actual Rust executable in Root's future stage; it never reopens Native binary payloads, invokes Cargo/an engine or evaluates view factors.

The copied `shape.py` is byte-exact final OriginalDataQA02. It revalidates actual Native seed/SPtr/class/ID/shape/callback/partial/error/warning/diagnostic integrity and derives the exact counts again. It does not predict source returns, warnings, areas or factors. `packet_io.py` is the accepted RAD IO105, byte-exact final QA02. All observation JSON here retains the existing 16000000-byte load bound and 64000000-byte identity bound; no observation-size expansion is introduced.

Pairing preserves all 21 literal row identities and declared unit lanes. Actual typed Rust registry and pointer-order owners retain the supplied opaque IDs, original names/classes/zone association and scalar input bits. Required Native and Rust invocations, successful source returns and complete returned owners must both be available. One-sided or both-sided absence, source stop, typed error or unreached required owner fails the selected comparison. Available native partial/stopped observations remain factual context and never substitute for returned owners. Matrix dimensions, vector lengths, returned context and ordered IDs are exact.

Two numerical profiles, `ZoneArea` and `F`, are frozen before outputs with `atol=0.0`, `rtol=0.0`, exact class/shape and exact signed-zero bits. The existing `Comparison` primitive is reused. Its sole arithmetic-policy delta is an explicit exact bit comparison when both actual values are zero. DTO validation, finite differences, maximum error and RMSE retain the established implementation; nonfinite actual values are retained with their class/bits but do not receive a numerical PASS. No visibility, area accumulation, matrix division, correction, expected buffer, fallback or warning predicate is computed.

Actual Native warning markers must match the actual Rust typed vector in count and order, source position, surface identity/name and zone identity/name. The conversion between Native one-based surface position and Rust zero-based position is explicit. Opaque IDs come from the actual Native seeded pointer snapshot, not from warning prediction or a numeric answer. Global Native diagnostic severity/text/log/counters remain separately retained context; the typed API has no backend delivery owner, and no equivalence of those messages is certified.

The report schema is `rad01-unit-comparison.v1`, with status `pass-selected-approximate-view-factors` or `fail-selected-approximate-view-factors`. `selected_declared_geometry_unit_PASS_claimed` depends on all required comparisons and both finite profile coverages. `complete_RAD01_PASS_claimed`, full-engine geometry, production integration, RAD-02/RAD-03, global diagnostic backend certification and gate updates remain false. Six CON-name template rows are declared unit geometry, never injected production fixtures. The old private F-only API remains explicitly unavailable as a public ZoneArea/warning baseline.

The six unexecuted `comparison_contract_tests.py` cases cover exact signed zero, equal negative zero, one-ULP strictness, nonfinite availability, both-required absence/empty profiles and malformed DTO rejection. They exercise only the existing comparison primitive with scalar values; they are not RAD expected answers or an extra QA/proof stage. This agent ran only stdlib metadata/hash/AST/diff authoring, and no target import, test, formatter, engine, scientific result or binary payload read.

Base authored the Native/Rust RAD arithmetic, Raw authored factual OriginalDataQA, and Header authored this observer/comparison adaptation. Full other-author source review and Root's independent review remain prerequisites. Actual same-input comparison is a later separate obligation, and no formula certificate or scientific completion is claimed here.

Fresh02 replaces only the approved factual QA03 manifest path/SHA, whose Native02/freezer03/current-successful-build scope pins supersede the failed-build ancestry. Comparator pairing/numeric/absence/warning logic, six unexecuted primitive tests and exact shape/IO copies remain byte-identical01. Current reader/dependency/range descriptors follow the reviewed successors; historical01 before/diffs remain authentic. No stage was imported or executed, and no policy or outcome was changed.
